{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/908197-unbreakable-confusion","id":908197,"title":"Unbreakable Confusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-06T01:00:49-07:00","id":908197,"title":"Unbreakable Confusion","content":"There's a clause at the end of Unbreakable's satiety expenditure effect that states <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">His armor (still 4/3) <b>applies to aggravated </b><b>damage attacks</b>.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>This is confusing as according to a strict reading of the armor rules and <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173\" target=\"_blank\">this post by Dave on 4chan</a> general armor already applies to aggravated damage. Is there supposed to be a clause stating that Unbreakable does not normally protect against agg?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:28:36-07:00","id":911527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/908197-unbreakable-confusion#post908197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a clause at the end of Unbreakable's satiety expenditure effect that states<br /> <br /> This is confusing as according to a strict reading of the armor rules and <a href=\"http://archive.4plebs.org/tg/thread/47059905/#47061173\" target=\"_blank\">this post by Dave on 4chan</a> general armor already applies to aggravated damage. Is there supposed to be a clause stating that Unbreakable does not normally protect against agg?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I saw this too, and unfortunately I have no idea what was intended. The idea that armor doesn't apply against aggravated damage is a really common misconception, and it's entirely possible that the writer was addressing that misconception, either to clear it up for others, or because they thought it was true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:33:06-07:00","id":911751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/908197-unbreakable-confusion?p=911527#post911527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I saw this too, and unfortunately I have no idea what was intended. The idea that armor doesn't apply against aggravated damage is a really common misconception, and it's entirely possible that the writer was addressing that misconception, either to clear it up for others, or because they thought it was true.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself wondering if the devs are on the same page on this matter. It seems odd that this would have made it to print if Matt himself wasn't under the impression that agg normally bypassed armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T11:39:23-07:00","id":911791,"title":"","content":"If I had to guess I'd say that is is a case of specific trumps general. If you are comparing Unbreakable to another power or ability that does agg and ignores armor, I would just rule that unbreakable's armor would stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1445-elesho","name":"elesho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:00:34-07:00","id":911805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cmwatford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/908197-unbreakable-confusion?p=911751#post911751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself wondering if the devs are on the same page on this matter. It seems odd that this would have made it to print if Matt himself wasn't under the impression that agg normally bypassed armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The conversation you cited earlier specifically referenced the fact that werewolves taking aggravated damage from silver didn't make silver bullets stop acting like bullets when they encountered a Kevlar vest, Unbreakable's primary hole is damage done by Anathema, and there are multiple Lair Traits that deal aggravated damage through a variety of vectors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T12:08:11-07:00","id":911812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/908197-unbreakable-confusion?p=911805#post911805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversation you cited earlier specifically referenced the fact that werewolves taking aggravated damage from silver didn't make silver bullets stop acting like bullets when they encountered a Kevlar vest, Unbreakable's primary hole is damage done by Anathema, and there are multiple Lair Traits that deal aggravated damage through a variety of vectors.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. So the interpretation we should run with is that Unbreakable applies to ALL agg, even that which would normally not be reduced by armor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}